        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-13T19:07:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there is an issue with this approach as there are up to 3 different registers that need to be modified.\n\nCtlTop:0x04 -\u003e FLIP and USB3 enable/disable\nCtlTop:0x05 -\u003e DP enable/disable\nCtlTop:0x06 -\u003e TBT/USB4 enable/disable\n\nAll this will use the same I2C address to access, but there are 3 registers to modify depending on the contents of mux_state.\n\nOne approach would be to keep 3 temporary variables here, initialized to 0. Then set bits in these temp variables as mux_state bits are checked. The masks for each of the 3 registers can be macros as they don\u0027t need to change. Then the ctltop_update function can do register read/modify/write using the masks for each fo the 3 registers. So you pass in 3 \u0027register content\u0027 arguments and not just one.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 143,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 143,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "4d92d6584273bee3090e5b41b0ab619e59a307e9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
